---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { me } from '../../../data.js';

const title = 'GrammarLens privacy policy';
const description = 'What data GrammarLens collects, where it goes, and how long it is kept.';
const updated = 'August 2026';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>Privacy</strong>
      GrammarLens for iOS<br />
      Last updated {updated}
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h1 class="display">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This describes what GrammarLens does with your information. It is written to be read, not to
        cover me legally.
      </p>
      <div class="todo">
        <p>
          <strong>Before publishing:</strong> every claim below has to match what the app actually
          does. Check each section against the code. An inaccurate privacy policy is worse than a
          vague one — and Apple's review team does read this page.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>01</strong>
      Who runs this
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>Who I am</h2>
      <p>
        GrammarLens is made by {me.name}, an independent developer based in Istanbul, Turkey. There
        is no company behind it. If you have a question about anything on this page, email
        <a href={`mailto:${me.email}`}>{me.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>02</strong>
      What is stored,<br />
      and where
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>What GrammarLens stores</h2>
      <p>
        Your practice history and settings are stored in a database on your own device. They are not
        uploaded to a server that I control, and I cannot read them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Deleting the app deletes this data. There is no backup on my side to delete separately.
      </p>
      <div class="todo">
        <p>
          <strong>Confirm:</strong> does the app create an account, use iCloud sync, or collect an
          email address anywhere? If yes, that has to be described here.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>03</strong>
      What leaves<br />
      your device
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>Text sent for analysis</h2>
      <p>
        To explain a mistake, GrammarLens sends the sentence you entered to a language model API run
        by Anthropic. That request is what produces the explanation you see. Without it the app
        cannot work.
      </p>
      <p>
        Do not enter passwords, financial details, medical information, or anything else you would
        not want processed by a third party. Enter sentences you want checked, and nothing more.
      </p>
      <div class="todo">
        <p>
          <strong>Confirm and complete:</strong> exactly what is included in each request — just the
          sentence, or also history and settings? Then read Anthropic's current API data-retention
          terms and state their retention period here, with a link.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>04</strong>
      Analytics and<br />
      tracking
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <div class="todo">
        <p>
          <strong>Decide, then write one of two things:</strong> if the app contains no analytics or
          crash-reporting SDK, say plainly that it collects no usage data and does not track you
          across apps. If it does contain one, name the tool, say what it collects, and link to its
          policy. This section must also match your App Store Connect privacy answers exactly.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>05</strong>
      Children
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        GrammarLens is not designed for children and I do not knowingly collect information from
        them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>06</strong>
      Your rights and<br />
      changes to this page
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h2>Your data, and changes here</h2>
      <p>
        Because your practice data stays on your device, you already control it — deleting the app
        removes it. If you want to ask anything about data handling, email
        <a href={`mailto:${me.email}`}>{me.email}</a> and I'll answer.
      </p>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, I'll update the date at the top of this page. Meaningful changes will
        also be noted in the app's release notes.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/products/grammarlens/support">Support page</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp;
        <a href="/products/grammarlens">GrammarLens</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
